Modelica source:
```modelica
connector Flange
  Real s;
  flow Real f;
end Flange;
model Element
  Flange flange_a;
  Flange flange_b;
end Element;
model Study
  Flange boundary;
  Element m1;
  Element sd1;
  Element m2;
equation
  connect(boundary, m1.flange_b);
  connect(m1.flange_b, sd1.flange_a);
  connect(sd1.flange_a, m2.flange_a);
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set formed by explicit connect statements in that scope that contains boundary.f.

Target:
boundary.f

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
